WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.600
Dr. Arnn: We all
have a common problem.

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:03.830
How do you live well?

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:07.680
Our well-being, our happiness,
depends upon how we do that.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.310
And the Nicomachean Ethics
is the first great book

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.760
written about that subject.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.630
And, in my belief, the
best book ever written.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.038
Why is ethics important?

00:00:16.038 --> 00:00:18.580
Student 1: Because we're trying
to figure out how to be good.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:19.790
Dr. Arnn: Good is important.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:23.570
Every action, and every
choice, and every inquiry

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.760
we seem to make for some good.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.500
Somebody give a
simple definition

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.340
of what it is to be ethical.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.820
Student 2: Ethical would
be to pursue a good life.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.620
Dr. Arnn: And get there, right?

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:38.090
The reason this book is to
be read is to become good.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.100
This is an urgent inquiry.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.650
We are the makers
of our character.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:46.190
The claim of this book
is that this is certainly

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:47.540
the way to live well.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:48.890
You can become awesome.

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.770
Start today.

